## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides; tier 2, so short)
- **G-1 delta (C1).** A path beyond the one, a document, product, package or config byte = **Blocker**; any removed line, an old row changed or loosened = **Major, class (d)**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or the commit message = **Blocker**; a second commit or a moved head = STOP; a Jira key or work number in an added line or the commit message = **Minor** (the PR body's `PCOMP-104` is a Note: Tuesday writes the squash text); non-ASCII or a tab in the added lines = **Major**.
- **G-2 the rows against mutants (C2).** *Classification rule (decide each green or red result by it):* a shape is **IN the family** when it appends to, replaces inside, duplicates, reorders or splits the write, redirect, DROP, cat or apply line, or inserts, deletes or changes a line between the check line and the apply line (the lines the ticket and the commission name); it is **OUT** when it touches only line 199, line 202, line 208, a line outside the fences, comment tolerance, or a second copy of the whole block. For an IN shape: **equivalent in bash** (C2e argv equal, or a spacing change of ASCII blanks) must be green (a refused equivalent edit is a **Note**: stricter than necessary, state it); **not equivalent** and red on a new row = pass; **not equivalent and green on all 13** = a finding of class (a), by consequence: **Major** if the edit makes the block silently apply nothing, apply other content, target another database, user or container, or print a status that lies; **Minor** if the argv shows it fails loudly or fails safe by a mechanism you state (the check refuses, bash stops before the apply, psql is handed an option it must reject; psql's answer is UNMEASURED and said so). A Done-when shape (A1 A2 A3x A5 A6a A6c A6d A7c A9) not red on a named new row = **Major, class (a)**; red on an OLD row = the shape was not green on the old file (**Note**, with the cell); A4, A7a, A7b not red on a new row = **Major**; a new row red at the document = **Major, class (c)**; a new row green under the defect its title names, or red only as "block not found" = **Major, class (b)**; an old-file red set not a subset of the new = **Major**; a regression shape (M32 U5 U7 U8 F1 F2 F4 F5 F6 F7 X1 X2 X3, A6b) no longer red on its old rows = **Major**; a control that cannot fail (c5, c6) = the run is DEAD (say so, NOT TESTED) and for c5 a **Major** of its own. For an OUT shape green on all 13 = **Note** with ticket text and the measurement, **even when its harm equals the ticket's A1** (a status line that prints 0 whatever psql did, for example `true` inserted after the apply line or line 208 replaced by `echo 0`): name that sameness so Tuesday can decide a follow-up; it is not a reason for NO GO round 1 (the commission's lane stops at the lines it names). `umask 077` deleted, changed or moved (the restore script file keeps the shell default mask): **Note**, pre-existing coverage gap in a document block, no product byte; **report the measurement and the consequence in one sentence, and do NOT stop for it** (Q-2). A survivor of the K-X family (a changed target: container, database, user, the redirect) that stays green = **Major** by the rule above (IN family, other target).
- **G-3 counts and CI (C3, C4).** The file other than 13 of 13, or the group other than main + 0 files + 3 tests, without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 3 = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head and zero on main = **Major**; a whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a failing check-run on the head = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional); an open alert on the PR ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** the commit author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact (see LANDING), the `hpsm` pinned-text lines, the pin paragraph of `DEPLOY.md` understating the test (lines 222 to 239: ticket text for a later card), the PR body's understatement of row G.
- **G-4 words (C5, C7).** A commit-message sentence a run does not carry = **Major (class e)**; a PR title or body sentence a run does not carry = **Minor** (Tuesday edits it). **A test `it` title that claims more than its row asserts** (the commission's own binding discipline: "no sentence of an added title may claim more than its row asserts"): **Minor** when the overclaim is wording about spacing (the title says "whole text", the row folds ASCII blanks, and the commit message, the PR body and the row's control comment say "spacing aside" or "other spacing is not refused": W as the builder's item 6), **Minor, class (b)** when C2c shows a green edit that the title says is refused (U+00A0, U+000D or U+000B appended or substituted: the title's "text added to one of them is refused" is false for it) with the fix shape in prose (compare after trimming only ASCII blanks and collapsing only runs of space and tab, so that every other character shows), **Major, class (b)** only if the false claim is about a pin that guards a Done-when shape. Title G: the same table. A builder claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number; a survivor outside the family = **Note** in FOR TUESDAY with the value that does it, not of the class.
- **G-5 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker or any Major of the class = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch; a second NO GO on this class is a STOP to Tuesday under the cap). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows; decisions in FOR TUESDAY). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional. A PR title or body wording is Tuesday's edit before landing, never a reason by itself to send the branch back. **Tier handoff (G2 to G1):** a Major whose consequence is "another target" or "silently applies other content" (G-2) goes to Tuesday as a STOP-with-measurement rather than a quiet NO GO, per the escalation line below.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 4.10 at the draft; panes of MPS and NexusAI are live). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, the `packages/db` group, any vitest over more than one file, the unit chain, the mutant battery. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, the clone, C4 polls, C5/C6/C7 reads). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b845/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b845/quarantine/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b845/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line. Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b845-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b845-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`; `npm ci` must be CACHED); record node, npm, vitest, tsc (RELAYED by the builder: node v22.23.2, npm 10.9.8, vitest 5.0.0, tsc 5.9.3). One image serves main and the head only if the lockfile blobs are equal (prove it by `rev-parse` of both). Budget (write it at Step 0, about 10): baseline file 1, base group 1, head file x3 plus rows alone 2, head group 1, mutant battery 2 (ONE node container that loops over the container's own `/repo` layer; the mutants need no database), unit chain 1, scratch typecheck 1. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b845-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

