## LANDING (Tuesday's, not the gate's; the gate quotes it in FOR TUESDAY and never runs it)
Composer lands by SQUASH, head-pinned, after the gate says GO or GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS and a real green scan of the head through the org ruleset (never bypassed, no alert dismissed). Source (the project's recorded practice for Composer code; the repo allows squash, merge commit and rebase): `1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md` line 1799 (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER, `sed -n 1799p`): "squash-merges PR #88 pinned to head 2da99cab after re-reading CodeQL and the checks. Nothing is deployed (Composer deploys only on your card)." The Composer project `CLAUDE.md` says the live demo site is the owner's: never deploy to it without the owner's word.
**The branch commit's author is a machine-local identity** (`<first name> <...@<hostname>.localdomain>`); earlier Composer squashes are authored by the GitHub noreply address with `Co-authored-by` trailers, and the squash `cbe86ba6` of #98 carries a trailer holding that machine-local kind of identity (MEASURED: its message contains `localdomain`). A default squash message would copy the same identity again. **So Tuesday writes the squash subject AND body explicitly and lands with:**
`gh pr merge 99 --squash --match-head-commit dc16530a9c3c4e484a54e8d2e01717bad31c355b --subject '<subject> (#99)' --body '<body>'`
- **Subject:** the commit title, `Route B test: pin the whole write, redirect and apply lines, each text once, and the order and closing of the group (#99)` (or the wording Tuesday settles from the gate's C5/G-4 grade of title W, which does not change the commit; the PR title is a public label only once the subject is explicit).
- **Body:** the two paragraphs of the commit message as the gate prints them at C5, then ONE attribution line `Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>` and **no other trailer**. No person's name, no ticket key, no work number in the body (the PR body's `PCOMP-104` stays in the PR).
- **Verify after the merge, before anything else is done with main:** `gh api -X GET repos/datasecau/Datasec-Security-Composer/commits/<squash sha> --jq .commit.message` (GET only): (i) `/usr/bin/grep -c -i 'co-authored-by'` = 1 and the one line is the noreply address; (ii) `/usr/bin/grep -c -i 'localdomain'` = **0** (control: the same read on `cbe86ba61a45ed776122bf4ee31fd682a0244c1a` prints 1); (iii) the subject is the one written; (iv) the squash commit's parent is the main that was merged against and **its tree equals the head's tree `938486687d8540391433256eea39f5e650372f99`** while main is `cbe86ba6` (if another PR landed first on other paths the tree differs by those paths, not by a conflict). **If (ii) is not 0 do not amend or rewrite main** (no force, no history edit): report it to the product owner as a finding about the landing and stop.
- A merge to main is not a deploy and Composer deploys only on the product owner's card. The records seat moves PCOMP-104 and writes the pin-paragraph word change as a later card.
